# No mito deploy / no process control

Never deploy code to mito. Never kill, start, or restart processes on mito.
Change code **only locally**. The user deploys and restarts manually.

This covers polybot-react and related backends worked from this workspace
(polycandles, mitobot, gobot, etc.).

## Forbidden

- SSH (or any remote) to **build, copy, install, restart, kill**, or run app binaries on mito
- `scp`, `rsync`, or writing source/binaries under `/root/prog/*`, `/mnt/polygon/*`, or similar
- `pkill`, `kill`, systemd, tmux, `nohup`, or any start/stop/restart of polycandles / mitobot / other mito apps
- Replacing binaries or swapping `*.new` / `*.prev` on the server
- Implied deploy after a local fix ("restart so it picks up changes")

## Allowed

- Edit, build, and test **locally**
- SSH only to **read** (logs, status, `grep`, `pgrep` for diagnosis) — never to change process or deploy
- Tell the user exact commands to run on mito if deploy/restart is needed

## After code changes

Stop at local work. Offer mito commands in chat; do **not** run them.

## Overrides

Only if the user **explicitly** asks in that message to deploy / kill / restart
on mito (e.g. "deploy polycandles", "kill polycandles on mito").
A code fix alone is not permission to deploy.
